Whether an item is in a list of integers. The input is the pair (x . xs); the output is Ok 1 if x is in xs, and Ok 0 if not.
---

---
fn p
	let x = (fst p)
	letrec c = fn l
		if (= (@ l) 1)
			(Ok 0)
		else
			let h = (head l)?
			if (= h x)
				(Ok 1)
			else
				let t = (tail l)?
				(c t)
	(c (snd p))
---
⟨2 [1 2 3]⟩ => Ok 1 fuel 1000
⟨9 [1 2 3]⟩ => Ok 0 fuel 1000
⟨1 ~⟩ => Ok 0 fuel 1000

